{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands","id":1372771,"title":"Gay and Lesbian Kingdom of the Coral Sea Islands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-04T11:57:18-08:00","id":1372771,"title":"Gay and Lesbian Kingdom of the Coral Sea Islands","content":"<img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/498704231407288320/684843012005691433/image0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> After looking at some RPG examples, it seems that in D&amp;D and other European medieval settings, places names are usually in a made-up language, a modified version of an existing word, or <i>extremely </i>descriptive English words (like the Wound Coast or The Forest of Doom for example). Which just doesn't resonate with me at all for some reason, they just feel somewhat fake and it's taking me out of the immersion.<br /> <br /> So I look at some examples from the real-world instead in my country, so there are:<br /> \u2022 Creating a name from local legends (Th\u0103ng Long is about the king seeing an ascending dragon for example).<br /> \u2022 There are also names taking after the village/city's founder.<br /> \u2022 After a geographic point nearby (\u010c\u01b0 Hu\u00ea means Mount Hue).<br /> \u2022 Or the shape of the land (C\u1eedu Long means Nine Dragons since there are nine rivers there.<br /> \u2022 And name that the current people just don't know the meaning of (which would be fitting for a made-up fantasy name).<br /> <br /> How do you guys choose a name for your homebrew locations? Since I'm having some serious trouble when it comes to this step even with examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T13:40:33-08:00","id":1372804,"title":"","content":"I mean, I usually just poke an appropriate random name generator that seems related until I get something that sounds good to me. Or go with extremely descriptive English, which seems fitting for Exalted if nothing else. That said, I do enjoy your map there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:43:44-08:00","id":1372832,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Nothing Interesting Isles are a ruse. I bet there is something very interesting there or at least one lone Exalt's mad search for that very thing might make it interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T17:40:57-08:00","id":1372855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1372832#post1372832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Nothing Interesting Isles are a ruse. I bet there is something very interesting there or at least one lone Exalt's mad search for that very thing might make it interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More like &quot;Someone Did Not Look Hard Enough Isles&quot;, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But on the topic, i usually do as you mentioned and just I look at some examples from the real-world in my own country and adapt a bit.<br /> <br /> For examples:<br /> - an old city/funeral district/shadowland area in a larger city called &quot;Good Repose&quot;.<br /> - a place called Greenmaw Valley, named so because a tribe of wyld barbarians that worship this sort of wood elementals, to the point of naming themselves after them, live there.<br /> - a pale, svelte, long-eared people known locally as &quot;bloodless&quot; or &quot;white lintha&quot;, for their descent from the modified mortal slaves/vassals of the Bugiber, or Red Lintha, a race of elfin inhuman reavers of unclear origins that in my games dominated a large expanse of the White Sea in the first century post-Contagion, until they crossed swords with the empire of Bagresh Kol, ending their time of terror (though not their race and threat per se).<br /> <br /> Frequently i make use of &quot;hook names&quot;, where something in a place or people's name, title or nicknames can serve as a clue to some other little facts the PCs can learn if they just ask. Greenmaw as a reference not only to the barbarians appearance but ties to the elementals, &quot;white lintha&quot; as a clue to the existence of their past masters and the Bugibers' similarities and obscure relation to the Lintha, or &quot;bloodless&quot; as a veiled reference to the Bugiber's obsession with blood-based magics and so on.<br /> <br /> Overall, it pans out well. quick to do &amp; understand, the players usually catch on quick and works fine in the &quot;make images stick on the players heads&quot; department.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-03-2024, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T22:51:57-08:00","id":1372905,"title":"","content":"I guess extremely descriptive English names are pretty easy to make compare to combing through dictionaries to make a non-English name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T23:03:20-08:00","id":1372906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1372905#post1372905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess extremely descriptive English names are pretty easy to make compare to combing through dictionaries to make a non-English name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, technically i use extremely descriptive <i>portuguese </i>names, but yeah, same principle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Simple, convenient, has some real world basis - and makes the weird pidgin letter soup ones even more notable by contrast, so what's not to like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-05-2020, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T23:32:04-08:00","id":1372909,"title":"","content":"How interesting, what would be an example of an extremely descriptive <i>portuguese </i>name, can they be the name of a real-place in Portugal?<br /> <br /> Since names in my language are usually using the Han character which ranges from super simple (T\u00e2y H\u1ed3 basically means Western Lake) to purple-prose like Hall of Eternal Autumn, but rarely the extremely descriptive kind (which probably explain why I have a hard time jive-ing with a name like Forest of Doom).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T04:41:00-08:00","id":1372935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1372832#post1372832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Nothing Interesting Isles are a ruse. I bet there is something very interesting there or at least one lone Exalt's mad search for that very thing might make it interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I noticed that these are supposedly the Gay and Lesbian Kingdoms, but all the names are gay-themed, rather than lesbian. One possible explanation of this is that the gay and lesbian cultures on the island actually speak different languages, and have different names for the locations. The Nothing Interesting Isles might be quite interesting to the other gender...<br /> <br /> I am no expert on lesbian puns but I have some ideas of Lots of Trees Forest and I Ran Out of Gay Words Sea might be called in the other language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T04:46:04-08:00","id":1372936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1372909#post1372909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How interesting, what would be an example of an extremely descriptive <i>portuguese </i>name, can they be the name of a real-place in Portugal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know how descriptive one would count it, but the shadowland/old city i mentioned is named <b><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bom_Retiro_(district_of_S%C3%A3o_Paulo)\" target=\"_blank\">Bom Retiro</a></i></b>, in a bit of wordplay as <i>retiro </i>in portuguese can be interpreted as rest, exile, retirement or repose depending on context.<br /> <br /> A better one might be <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Po%C3%A7os_de_Caldas\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Po\u00e7os de Caldas</i></b></a> (literally &quot;Calderas Springs&quot;), a city known for its thermal baths in the State of Minas Gerais (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minas_Gerais#Etymology\" target=\"_blank\">that might or not also count</a>, by the way).<br /> <br /> Places in Portugal that would fit the bill most probably exist, but i'm far more familiar with brazilian ones. What can i say, it happens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-05-2020, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T05:34:11-08:00","id":1372944,"title":"","content":"I mostly do &quot;major geographic feature&quot; &quot;name of important person&quot; or &quot;folk named&quot;<br /> Twin Split Spears is named after two giant monoliths of stone, pointed at the top, that rise from the ground. Local belief has it that the first humans (or at least the first warriors) emerged fromt he split spears.<br /> Sukulit's name is lost to history, but generally accepted to be connected to the ruin that stands here. It's actual derivation is from an Old Realm phrase &quot;Watcher Upon the Shore&quot;, as the First Age city was also watching an ancient broken Solar Working that was refusing to die properly.<br /> Yirji is named after the local family of snake gods.<br /> Five Phases Monastary or 108 Devils in Chains Monastary is (if I remember right) a shamless reference ot Journey to the west and also reflective of local folk belief that the monastary has 108 demons imprisoned in statues in their halls (its 107, actually--108 is under the mountain)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T16:41:18-08:00","id":1373095,"title":"","content":"Some real world examples - <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/ps1Awyv\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/a/ps1Awyv</a> <br /> <br /> (Though I suspect some liberties have been taken with some of these - the last is from Gene's Wolfe's Latro sequence, and I *know* he stylized it a bit!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T11:34:02-08:00","id":1373234,"title":"","content":"I don't have a specific naming convention I follow, I just make sure to google everything to make sure it's not distracting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T15:26:40-08:00","id":1373271,"title":"","content":"I am extremely disappointed by the bait and switch that is this thread, I know you can do better than that Jen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T21:14:32-08:00","id":1373321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1373271#post1373271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am extremely disappointed by the bait and switch that is this thread, I know you can do better than that Jen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Jen threads. First time? lol. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1372905#post1372905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess extremely descriptive English names are pretty easy to make compare to combing through dictionaries to make a non-English name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Japanese is even worse about this. From Kyoto to Himeji, here is a translated list of major cities: Capital City, Big Slope, Western Shrine, God's Door, Bright Rock, High Sand, Waterfall, Old River, Princess Path. Western Shrine has a shrine in it west of the city. Princess Path is where a princess lived. Big Slope is built on a big slope. <br /> <br /> Big Slope's major downtown district is called Plum Field, but actually it used to be Buried Field but they thought that sounded grim so they changed the kanji. I live in a part of a city called East Town. My friends live by Swamp Lake and, roughly translated, &quot;That place where the fish are&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T23:38:26-08:00","id":1373329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1373271#post1373271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am extremely disappointed by the bait and switch that is this thread, I know you can do better than that Jen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll create a thread with actual gay furry content someday<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372771-gay-and-lesbian-kingdom-of-the-coral-sea-islands?p=1373321#post1373321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Japanese is even worse about this. From Kyoto to Himeji, here is a translated list of major cities: Capital City, Big Slope, Western Shrine, God's Door, Bright Rock, High Sand, Waterfall, Old River, Princess Path. Western Shrine has a shrine in it west of the city. Princess Path is where a princess lived. Big Slope is built on a big slope.<br /> <br /> Big Slope's major downtown district is called Plum Field, but actually it used to be Buried Field but they thought that sounded grim so they changed the kanji. I live in a part of a city called East Town. My friends live by Swamp Lake and, roughly translated, &quot;That place where the fish are&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought the Romaji names look pretty exotic, but then I look at the kanji and lots of them are super &quot;The lake in the west is called Western Lake&quot;. Though I have the feeling that they will only sound in-your-face if you translate them into English or actively thinking about the meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T02:33:58-08:00","id":1373346,"title":"","content":"Chinese is the same too; the capital is called &quot;North Capital&quot;. A lot of provinces are &quot;east of the mountain&quot; &quot;west of the mountain&quot;, etc. Though I used to live in Black Dragon River province, which is cool.<br /> <br /> Tbh, as I live in Britain and so am used to place-names which are evolutions of words in multiple different languages 1500 years ago, I use a mix of nonsense words I like the sound of, or descriptive things I think are cool.<br /> I'll show some examples in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T09:11:26-08:00","id":1373389,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://postimg.cc/fJt523q1\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/fJt523q1/Final-map-of-The-Twisted-Fang.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://postimg.cc/RW17yw7p\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/RW17yw7p/Paint-map-of-Icehaven-Valley.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> So, basically, the names are a mix of descriptive ones (but ones I think sound good, not just &quot;East Forest&quot; or whatever) and nonsense words I think sound cool and appropriate for the area, and the occasional one that's deliberately chosen. In this case, Caer Moroth; Caer is Welsh for castle, which is the root of Camelot (Caer Melot). So basically, it sounds like Camelot, I just changed it a bit to not be too overt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-07-2020, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T14:34:05-08:00","id":1373438,"title":"","content":"When the direction naming scheme doesn't match, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/5Z3YC3NzNzU?t=24\" target=\"_blank\">things can get confusing...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}